{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "06U5", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-submersive}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:050e8438beb02f100cd55559ec6ade07ccdd86c564f5959674aed39eedbb385d", "source_text": "Submersive morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ebf3b297db60b27daa6dbae32db6caa15dfe0cfdd9ff315c5c247b02528116d5", "unit_id": "tag:06U5:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06U5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-properties-morphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dfaee67d46ddd4d888702445be4244f6d5bf5b01389aeba0ea95707e8ecf77c4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2cd80316ff7abc3d9a1f7eea97d38e305c6586e1073808e141a6d584dc9aac6a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks which is representable by\nalgebraic spaces. In\nProperties of Stacks, Section\n<REF_0001>\nwe have defined what it means for <MATH_0002> to be universally submersive.\nHere is another characterization.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:472bafd694b063b161f1b98d1b9ca2811c73e3377945f26e39b5fdc152c8318a", "unit_id": "tag:06U5:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06U5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$|\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\to |\\mathcal{Z}|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-properties-morphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-representable-universally-submersive}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9d5aeb9363e6c0460c4d8ca174db9b6e52fab48bca0eb728566dbe3f6bc86cf4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:549436c09606c225c605a10e1018e296bd4b5ec0b059fec75dc2f7117218f8b7", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of\nalgebraic stacks which is representable by algebraic spaces.\nThe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is universally submersive (as in Properties of Stacks,\nSection <REF_0001>), and\n<STRUCT_0003> for every morphism of algebraic stacks <MATH_0003>\nthe morphism of topological spaces\n<MATH_0004> is submersive.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:58c41ce8c3bda0d49bbf59ec790c95b6dfdcf3b79f79f6427ee02a5108689fe9", "unit_id": "tag:0CHX:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06U5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$V$", "MATH_0003": "$V \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0004": "$V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to V$", "MATH_0005": "$|V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\to |V|$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n|V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\n|\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\ar[d] \\\\\n|V| \\ar[r] & |\\mathcal{Z}|\n}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n|V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\longrightarrow\n|V| \\times_{|\\mathcal{Z}|} |\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}|\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Rightarrow$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-points}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:09aa1f8c8ad23cd19dc339d90766602caa1ad31ba2d799a54bf34d02f2619393", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3e551a9fbcd1f0ea5579f5a6d27b72b5baa602f38096bfccacb164889b8df9d5", "source_text": "Assume (1), and let <MATH_0001> be as in (2).\nChoose a scheme <MATH_0002> and a surjective smooth morphism <MATH_0003>.\nBy assumption the morphism <MATH_0004>\nof algebraic spaces is universally submersive, in particular the map\n<MATH_0005> is submersive. By\nProperties of Stacks, Section <REF_0001>\nin the commutative diagram\n<MATH_0006>\nthe horizontal arrows are open and surjective, and moreover\n<MATH_0007>\nis surjective. Hence as the left vertical arrow is submersive it follows that\nthe right vertical arrow is submersive. This proves (2).\nThe implication (2) <MATH_0008> (1) follows from the definitions.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7c910c17551c0b12d602d65add301cba70051f0a9912b0c78cd20602ed5969ba", "unit_id": "tag:0CHX:proof"}
